--------------------------------------------------------------------
THE 1995 DESKTOP LOOK  -  independent recreation
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The window chrome, the cursors and the desktop metaphor are an
independent recreation of a mid-1990s graphical interface. NO
MICROSOFT ASSET IS USED, AND NONE MAY BE ADDED.

What that means in practice:

  THE LOOK is not owned by anyone. Copyright protects expression, not
  visual style. Grey bevelled panels, a coloured title bar, inset
  borders and a close box are an aesthetic, and an aesthetic cannot be
  owned. Recreating one is as legitimate as designing a site to look
  like a newspaper.

  THE WINDOW CHROME here is CSS: hex colours and box-shadow insets
  (#c0c0c0, #000082, inset 1px bevels). There is no imported bitmap,
  no icon file, no theme package, no third-party stylesheet.

  THE CURSORS are original pixel art, drawn in tools/cursors.py as
  ASCII and generated to PNG. An arrow, a pointing hand, an open hand,
  a fist and a no-entry sign are generic interface symbols that predate
  Windows by a decade.

  THE TYPEFACE is Inter Tight under the SIL Open Font License 1.1,
  self-hosted. No Microsoft font is used or referenced.

  NO TRADEMARK is used. The dialog is labelled "System message". The
  words Windows and Microsoft, and the four-pane logo, appear nowhere,
  and nothing here implies endorsement by or association with anyone.

RULES FOR ANYONE WORKING ON THIS
--------------------------------
